From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 03:06:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 06/45] inkling2: attention partials start at the call's first
 chunk

Partials were indexed by absolute chunk, so a sliding layer at depth sized
them for every chunk up to the position: 4,096 at 1M, about 100 MB a prompt
row. Each call now passes its earliest row's first chunk and launches only
the chunks its rows read (at most 4-5 for a decode row on a sliding layer).
Chunk boundaries stay absolute, so the bits do not change: the 2-layer pack's
logits are byte-identical before and after on every text and path.
---
